IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc11-punishment`
IMPORT `ccc11-orders`

-- orders: tests of ccc11-orders.l4 (Part VIII.1, sections 320.23 to 320.25: delay of sentencing, prohibition orders, stay pending appeal)
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the provision, beside each assertion, before the run; none is copied from the code's output.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING: the text says yes / the text says no in its own words / not covered.

GIVEN p IS A `s 320.24(2) prohibition period`
GIVETH A `Length of time`
`s 320.24 test: not less than` MEANS p's `s 320.24 not less than`

GIVEN p IS A `s 320.24(2) prohibition period`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Length of time`)
`s 320.24 test: not more than` MEANS p's `s 320.24 not more than`

GIVEN p IS A `s 320.24(2) prohibition period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 320.24 test: plus the entire period` MEANS p's `s 320.24 plus the entire period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment`

§ `s 320.23(1): the offences named by number (320.14(1), with its paragraphs, and 320.15(1))`
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.14, "(1)") EQUALS TRUE   -- 320.14(1)
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.14, "(1)(d)") EQUALS TRUE   -- a paragraph of 320.14(1)
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.15, "(1)") EQUALS TRUE   -- 320.15(1)
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.14, "(2)") EQUALS FALSE   -- 320.14(2) is another offence
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.15, "(2)") EQUALS FALSE   -- 320.15(2) is another offence
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.13, "(1)") EQUALS FALSE   -- dangerous operation is not named
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.14, "(4)") EQUALS FALSE   -- 320.14(4) is not named
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the offence is an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.16, "(1)") EQUALS FALSE   -- 320.16(1) is not named

§ `s 320.23(1): the court may delay sentencing (a power with no "if" gate: a consent not given or the interests of justice not considered is JUST FALSE, listed fork F34; outside its scope NOT COVERED), and the duty that follows`
-- arguments: found guilty of an offence under 320.14(1) or 320.15(1) ; the prosecutor consents ; the offender consents ; the court has considered the interests of justice ; the delay is to attend an approved treatment program
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all gates
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not found guilty of such an offence
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 lists the power to delay (conditions of the with/after kind) with the guide's JUST FALSE where a consent is not given or the interests of justice are not considered (fork F34)
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 lists the power to delay (conditions of the with/after kind) with the guide's JUST FALSE where a consent is not given or the interests of justice are not considered (fork F34)
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 lists the power to delay (conditions of the with/after kind) with the guide's JUST FALSE where a consent is not given or the interests of justice are not considered (fork F34)
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not found guilty of such an offence and the prosecutor does not consent: a no beats a not-covered
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court may delay sentencing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not to attend a treatment program: a scope limit, not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the court delays sentencing: it "shall make an order prohibiting"
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no delay: the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) subsections 320.24(6) to (9) apply to the order made before sentencing` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- such an order has been made: subsections 320.24(6) to (9) apply
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) subsections 320.24(6) to (9) apply to the order made before sentencing` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no such order
#ASSERT `s 320.23(1) the court shall make a prohibition order before sentencing` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED   -- no delay, no duty: FULFILLED
-- The duty as a regulative rule: a trace is printed, not asserted (the stable binary cannot compare an open obligation; NOTES.md).
#TRACE `s 320.23(1) the court shall make a prohibition order before sentencing` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 320.23(1) make an order prohibiting the offender from operating, before sentencing, the type of conveyance in question` AT 1

§ `s 320.23(2): on completion of the treatment program the court is not required to impose the minimum punishment or make a prohibition order, but shall not direct a discharge`
#ASSERT `s 320.23(2) the court is not required to impose the minimum punishment under section 320.19 or to make a prohibition order under section 320.24` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- completed the program
#ASSERT `s 320.23(2) the court is not required to impose the minimum punishment under section 320.19 or to make a prohibition order under section 320.24` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not completed: no relief on these facts
#ASSERT `s 320.23(2) this subsection bars the court from directing a discharge under section 730` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- completed: the court shall not direct a discharge under 730
#ASSERT `s 320.23(2) this subsection bars the court from directing a discharge under section 730` FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not completed: this subsection does not bar a discharge

§ `s 320.24(1): the court shall make a prohibition order after a finding of guilt under 320.14(1) or 320.15(1), subject to 320.23(2)`
-- arguments: found guilty of an offence under 320.14(1) or 320.15(1) ; the court is not required, by 320.23(2)
#ASSERT `s 320.24(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- found guilty, no relief under 320.23(2)
#ASSERT `s 320.24(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the treatment program was completed: "the court is not required ... to make a prohibition order"
#ASSERT `s 320.24(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether 320.23(2) relieves the court is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.24(1) the court shall make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not found guilty of such an offence: the "if" is unmet
#ASSERT `s 320.24(1) the court shall make a prohibition order` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED   -- no finding of guilt: no duty
#TRACE `s 320.24(1) the court shall make a prohibition order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 320.24(1) make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` AT 1

§ `s 320.24(2): the prohibition period by occasion (plus the entire period of imprisonment)`
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not less than` (`s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` `s 320.19 a first offence`) EQUALS `Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE   -- (a) first offence: not less than one year
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` `s 320.19 a first offence`) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (a): not more than three years
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: plus the entire period` (`s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` `s 320.19 a first offence`) EQUALS TRUE   -- (a): plus the entire period of imprisonment
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not less than` (`s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` `s 320.19 a second offence`) EQUALS `Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE   -- (b) second offence: not less than two years
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` `s 320.19 a second offence`) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (b): not more than 10 years
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not less than` (`s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` `s 320.19 a subsequent offence`) EQUALS `Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE   -- (c) subsequent: not less than three years
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` `s 320.19 a subsequent offence`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- (c): no maximum is stated
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: plus the entire period` (`s 320.24(2) the prohibition period` `s 320.19 a subsequent offence`) EQUALS TRUE   -- (c): plus the entire period of imprisonment

§ `s 320.24(3): after a finding of guilt under 320.14(4) the court may prohibit for not more than one year (a power)`
#ASSERT `s 320.24(3) the longest period for which the court may prohibit the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- found guilty under 320.14(4): up to one year
#ASSERT `s 320.24(3) the longest period for which the court may prohibit the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not found guilty under 320.14(4): not covered

§ `s 320.24(4): the offences listed by number (sections 220, 221, 236, 320.13; 320.14(2) and (3); 320.15(2) and (3); 320.16 to 320.18)`
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 220, "") EQUALS TRUE   -- section 220
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 221, "") EQUALS TRUE   -- section 221
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 236, "") EQUALS TRUE   -- section 236
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.13, "(2)") EQUALS TRUE   -- section 320.13 (whole)
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.14, "(2)") EQUALS TRUE   -- 320.14(2)
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.14, "(3)") EQUALS TRUE   -- 320.14(3)
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.14, "(1)") EQUALS FALSE   -- 320.14(1) is the mandatory order's (subsection (1)), not listed in (4)
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.14, "(4)") EQUALS FALSE   -- 320.14(4) is subsection (3)'s
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.15, "(2)") EQUALS TRUE   -- 320.15(2)
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.15, "(1)") EQUALS FALSE   -- 320.15(1) is not listed in (4)
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.16, "(1)") EQUALS TRUE   -- the first of sections 320.16 to 320.18
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.17, "") EQUALS TRUE   -- inside 320.16 to 320.18
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.18, "(1)") EQUALS TRUE   -- the last of them
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.19, "(1)") EQUALS FALSE   -- just after the range
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 320.12, "") EQUALS FALSE   -- before 320.13
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the offence is one of the offences listed in subsection 320.24(4)` (`Provision of the Code` OF 222, "") EQUALS FALSE   -- section 222 is not listed
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- found guilty of a listed offence
#ASSERT `s 320.24(4) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from operating the type of conveyance in question` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a listed offence: not covered

§ `s 320.24(5): the period of a discretionary order by the maximum imprisonment the offender is liable to`
-- argument: the maximum imprisonment the offender is liable to in respect of that offence
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` `imprisonment for life`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a) life: any duration the court considers appropriate: no maximum is stated
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not less than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` `imprisonment for life`) EQUALS `Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE   -- no minimum is stated
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (b) more than five years but less than life: not more than 10 years
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 6, 0, 0, FALSE))) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (b) six years
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 1, FALSE))) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (b) five years and a day is more than five years
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 1, 0, FALSE))) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 10, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (b) five years and a month
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (c) exactly five years is not "more than five years"
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 4, 0, 0, FALSE))) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (c) four years
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`)) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (c) two years less a day
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: not more than` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` `no imprisonment is stated`) EQUALS JUST (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE)   -- (c) any other case
#ASSERT `s 320.24 test: plus the entire period` (`s 320.24(5) the prohibition period for a discretionary order` `imprisonment for life`) EQUALS TRUE   -- each period is plus the entire period of imprisonment

§ `s 320.24(5.1): a prohibition order takes effect on the day it is made, subject to a consecutive order under (9)`
#ASSERT `s 320.24(5.1) the day on which the prohibition order takes effect` (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)   -- takes effect the day it is made
#ASSERT `s 320.24(5.1) the day on which the prohibition order takes effect` (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- consecutive order: the text does not say on which day it then takes effect

§ `s 320.24(6) and (7): the duty to cause the order to be read or a copy given; the validity of the order does not depend on it`
-- arguments: the court makes a prohibition order ; the court causes the order to be read or a copy given
#ASSERT `s 320.24(6) the court has met its obligation to cause the order to be read or a copy to be given` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- order made and read or copy given
#ASSERT `s 320.24(6) the court has met its obligation to cause the order to be read or a copy to be given` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- order made and not read and no copy given
#ASSERT `s 320.24(6) the court has met its obligation to cause the order to be read or a copy to be given` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no order made: the obligation does not arise
#ASSERT `s 320.24(6) the court shall cause the order to be read or a copy to be given` FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED   -- no order made, no duty
#TRACE `s 320.24(6) the court shall cause the order to be read or a copy to be given` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 320.24(6) cause the order to be read by or to the offender or a copy of the order to be given to the offender` AT 1
#ASSERT `s 320.24(7) a failure to comply with subsection 320.24(6) affects the validity of the prohibition order` TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the failure does not affect the validity of the prohibition order
#ASSERT `s 320.24(7) a failure to comply with subsection 320.24(6) affects the validity of the prohibition order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no failure: the subsection is silent

§ `s 320.24(8): an order in respect of a motor vehicle applies only to its operation on a street, road, highway or other public place`
-- arguments: the order is in respect of a motor vehicle (by s 2) ; the operation is in a public place
#ASSERT `s 320.24(8) the prohibition order applies to the operation of the motor vehicle` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a motor vehicle, on a public road
#ASSERT `s 320.24(8) the prohibition order applies to the operation of the motor vehicle` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- a motor vehicle on private land: "applies only to"
#ASSERT `s 320.24(8) the prohibition order applies to the operation of the motor vehicle` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a motor vehicle: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `s 320.24(8) the prohibition order applies to the operation of the motor vehicle` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether it is a motor vehicle is not covered

§ `s 320.24(9): consecutive prohibition periods (a power)`
#ASSERT `s 320.24(9) the court may order that the prohibition order be served consecutively to the earlier order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- subject to an earlier order at the time of the offence, same type of conveyance
#ASSERT `s 320.24(9) the court may order that the prohibition order be served consecutively to the earlier order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not subject to an earlier order: not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.24(9) the court may order that the prohibition order be served consecutively to the earlier order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a different type of conveyance: not covered

§ `s 320.24(10): not registered in an interlock program until the expiry of the period (an "until" bar: before the expiry JUST TRUE, after it JUST FALSE)`
-- arguments: occasion ; the day the sentence is imposed ; the period fixed by order of the court, in months, if any ; the day asked about
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a first offence` (Date 15 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- first offence, no period fixed: "a period, if any": no bar
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a first offence` (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST 4) (Date 15 5 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- first offence, four months fixed: the bar runs through the day four months after
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a first offence` (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST 4) (Date 16 5 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the day after the period ends
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a second offence` (Date 15 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 4 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- second offence: three months after the day of sentence: still barred on that day
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a second offence` (Date 15 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 16 4 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the day after three months
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a second offence` (Date 15 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the day of sentence
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a second offence` (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST 5) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a longer period fixed by the court (five months) governs
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a second offence` (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST 5) (Date 16 6 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- after the longer period
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a second offence` (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST 2) (Date 16 4 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- a shorter fixed period does not shorten the three months, but 16 April is after them
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a second offence` (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST 2) (Date 15 4 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a shorter fixed period does not shorten the three months
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a subsequent offence` (Date 15 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 7 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- subsequent offence: six months
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a subsequent offence` (Date 15 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 16 7 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the day after six months
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a subsequent offence` (Date 15 1 2026) (JUST 8) (Date 15 9 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a longer period fixed by the court (eight months)
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a second offence` (Date 15 11 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 2 2027) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- three months from November rolls into the next year
#ASSERT `s 320.24(10) the person may not yet be registered in an alcohol ignition interlock device program` `s 320.19 a second offence` (Date 15 11 2026) NOTHING (Date 16 2 2027) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the day after

§ `s 320.25: stay of the prohibition order pending appeal`
-- arguments for (2): the appeal is to the Supreme Court of Canada ; the judge is a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken
#ASSERT `s 320.25(2) a direction may be made by this judge on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a Supreme Court of Canada appeal, a judge of the court appealed from
#ASSERT `s 320.25(2) a direction may be made by this judge on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- "only by a judge of the court from which the appeal was taken"
#ASSERT `s 320.25(2) a direction may be made by this judge on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 320.25(2) a direction may be made by this judge on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the sweep lists the "in the case of" gate of 320.25(2) with the guide's JUST FALSE on an appeal that is not to the Supreme Court of Canada (fork F35)
#ASSERT `s 320.25(2) a direction may be made by this judge on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 320.25(2) a direction may be made by this judge on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the sweep lists the "in the case of" gate of 320.25(2) with the guide's JUST FALSE on an appeal that is not to the Supreme Court of Canada (fork F35)
-- arguments for (1): the offence is under 320.13 to 320.18 (by s 320.22) ; an appeal is taken against the conviction or sentence ; the judge is of the court to which the appeal is taken ; the appeal is to the Supreme Court of Canada ; subsection (2) allows this judge (by s 320.25(2); consulted only on an appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada)
